{
  "id": "qud-data",
  "title": {
    "en": "Data Analysis & Probability",
    "ar": null
  },
  "content": {
    "blocks": [
      {
        "kind": "text",
        "body": {
          "en": "Reading values from tables and charts, summarising with mean, median and mode, and computing simple probabilities.",
          "ar": null
        }
      },
      {
        "kind": "callout",
        "style": "thm",
        "label": {
          "en": "▲ Reference — Summaries & chance",
          "ar": null
        },
        "body": {
          "en": "Mean is the total divided by the count; the median is the middle of the ordered list; the mode is the most frequent value. Probability of an event is \\( \\dfrac{\\text{favourable}}{\\text{total}} \\).",
          "ar": null
        }
      },
      {
        "kind": "cards",
        "items": [
          {
            "label": {
              "en": "Mean",
              "ar": null
            },
            "value": {
              "en": "\\( \\dfrac{\\text{sum}}{\\text{count}} \\)",
              "ar": null
            }
          },
          {
            "label": {
              "en": "Median",
              "ar": null
            },
            "value": {
              "en": "middle (ordered)",
              "ar": null
            }
          },
          {
            "label": {
              "en": "Mode",
              "ar": null
            },
            "value": {
              "en": "most frequent",
              "ar": null
            }
          },
          {
            "label": {
              "en": "Probability",
              "ar": null
            },
            "value": {
              "en": "\\( \\dfrac{\\text{favourable}}{\\text{total}} \\)",
              "ar": null
            }
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "kind": "callout",
        "style": "example",
        "label": {
          "en": "Worked example 7.A",
          "ar": null
        },
        "body": {
          "en": "Find the mean of \\( 4,\\,6,\\,8,\\,10,\\,12 \\). \\[ \\frac{40}{5}=8. \\]",
          "ar": null
        }
      },
      {
        "kind": "callout",
        "style": "example",
        "label": {
          "en": "Worked example 7.B",
          "ar": null
        },
        "body": {
          "en": "A bag holds 2 red and 3 green balls. Find \\( P(\\text{red}) \\). \\[ \\frac{2}{5}. \\]",
          "ar": null
        }
      },
      {
        "kind": "callout",
        "style": "warn",
        "label": {
          "en": "Practice Problem",
          "ar": null
        },
        "body": {
          "en": "Ages of 7 students: 14, 16, 14, 17, 15, 14, 18. Find mean, median, and mode. <details><summary>Show solution</summary><div>Ordered: 14,14,14,15,16,17,18. Mean\\(=108/7\\approx15.4.\\) Median\\(=15\\) (4th value). Mode\\(=14.\\)</div></details>",
          "ar": null
        }
      }
    ]
  },
  "quizWidget": {
    "enabled": true
  }
}
